 I don't see the elements not being discovered a huge deal, since they
are only used to name the description of wands.  If the properties of
the elements had any function at all in the game I could see a
stronger argument argument against them.  (Putting a uranium wand in a
bag of holding leads to an uncontrolled nuclear reaction, and so
forth).

I see the point in the argument against preserving food in tins. I
forgot about the "tin opener"; If the tinning kit doesn't constitute
advanced technology, I guess that certainly should.  It'd be like
finding a spork or swiss army knife.  Otherwise preserving food with
spices, inside  air-tight containers (ice box?), or with some
combination of that and "magic" doesn't seem so much of a stretch,
however.

If something not being discovered by a certain time period is an
argument against it appearing in the game, Neanderthals and maybe
cavemen in general might be precluded.  Also that whole crashed
spaceship level has always been a little suspect.



